      <div class="key-points">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Aroma type (香型) is the primary classification of baijiu, and it predicts flavour better than brand, price, or packaging.</li>
          <li>Twelve types are recognised; six account for nearly all internationally available bottles.</li>
          <li>Each type is tied to a national standard code printed on the back label — the fastest way to know what you are buying.</li>
          <li>Strong aroma is the biggest category by volume. Sauce aroma is the most famous. Light aroma is the most accessible.</li>
          <li>Aroma type does not predict quality. Excellent and poor bottles exist inside every category.</li>
        </ul>
